      "explanation": "In S<sub>N</sub>1 substitution reaction, reactivity of compound depends on the stability of carbocation formed in the rate determination step. Reactivity of compound will be more when it's carbocation is more stable.\n<br><br><picture><source media=\"(max-width: 320px)\" srcset=\"https://imagex.cdn.examgoal.net/jf76htyjzrdhjhy/1a11d835-bce3-4a69-a0d9-d9b4058741aa/84f81960-c76f-11e9-8a74-7f4f47aa0c85/file-jf76htyjzrdhjhz-320w.jpg\"><source media=\"(max-width: 500px)\" srcset=\"https://imagex.cdn.examgoal.net/jf76htyjzrdhjhy/1a11d835-bce3-4a69-a0d9-d9b4058741aa/84f81960-c76f-11e9-8a74-7f4f47aa0c85/file-jf76htyjzrdhjhz-500w.jpg\"><img src=\"https://imagex.cdn.examgoal.net/jf76htyjzrdhjhy/1a11d835-bce3-4a69-a0d9-d9b4058741aa/84f81960-c76f-11e9-8a74-7f4f47aa0c85/file-jf76htyjzrdhjhz-680w.jpg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;height: auto;display: block;margin: 0 auto;\" loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"JEE Main 2019 (Online) 9th April Evening Slot Chemistry - Hydrocarbons Question 133 English Explanation\"></picture>\n<br><br>So stability order of carbocation :\n<br><br>C &gt; D &gt; A &gt; B\n"
